    "FinDist_insertions": [
      {
        "head_range": [
          29,
          29
        ],
        "raw": "* `FinDist.probTrue p D`: the probability that the test `D` accepts a sample of `p`.\n",
        "raw_sha256": "0ab9fa32f1b9ed9fc65fd637f61e4c5143e48a68daa347c10179288f6c9f2cca"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          63,
          64
        ],
        "raw": "/-- The distribution built from weights `f` gives each outcome its weight:\n`⟨f, h₁, h₂⟩ a = f a`. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "c1768ffb7fbd24ab8dc373bd2dfa0d3398c33dfd555bb6cf332b45b92dabbf27"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          68,
          68
        ],
        "raw": "/-- Two distributions are equal when they give every outcome the same probability. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "840a2329c05526d4159f5bd7e4b87cc73c460c10477025d191f380c80e6f875b"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          72,
          72
        ],
        "raw": "/-- Every outcome has probability at most `1`. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "9d5fa50118f8bad8d54d1ca903b3fe5d70f3f62bd3226d91df96349f0ff6d7be"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          77,
          77
        ],
        "raw": "/-- A finite type that carries a distribution has positive cardinality. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "251fb32ee27aa22ed482223353b42cee51e989da8da20c8522c23010e099bb50"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          97,
          97
        ],
        "raw": "/-- The uniform distribution gives every outcome probability `|α|⁻¹`. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "673bf1b362261b5faf5361072aac550c311c9b474bd0242fbce34ee53494eb55"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          109,
          110
        ],
        "raw": "/-- The pushforward of `p` along `f` gives `b` the total probability of its preimage:\n`map f p b = ∑_{a : f a = b} p a`. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "546287dae5f3281680f8aca1c15bb8dcaed04756d2a4ee7ee22192f320be34e6"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          122,
          123
        ],
        "raw": "/-- The product distribution gives a pair the product of its coordinates' probabilities:\n`prod p q (a, b) = p a · q b`. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "a5d08bdca92066ceb1af9bddbdacd2a3ac6f56dcb87026f3bf593f0410a2ec31"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          131,
          131
        ],
        "raw": "/-- The collision probability is nonnegative. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "e1f706bf89885a4291d4e844c2370d64c2cc532a249bad3e370e4e2b77ba8c5e"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          135,
          135
        ],
        "raw": "/-- The uniform distribution has collision probability `|α|⁻¹`. -/\n",
        "raw_sha256": "a1cd777adae9c2c0e7ee237afd43b22fcd352cd55852f4a8beb4a024720a8efb"
      },
      {
        "head_range": [
          170,
          189
        ],
        "raw": "/-! ### Acceptance probability of a test -/\n\nvariable {α : Type*} [Fintype α]\n\n/-- The probability that the test `D` outputs `1` (`true`) on a sample of `p`:\n`Pr[x ← p : D(x) = 1]`. -/\nnoncomputable def FinDist.probTrue (p : FinDist α) (D : α → Bool) : ℝ :=\n  ∑ a ∈ univ.filter (fun a => D a = true), p a\n\n/-- The signed difference of two acceptance probabilities, `Pr_p[D = 1] - Pr_q[D = 1]`, is the\nsum of the probability differences `p a - q a` over the points `D` accepts. -/\ntheorem FinDist.probTrue_sub_probTrue (p q : FinDist α) (D : α → Bool) :\n    p.probTrue D - q.probTrue D = ∑ a ∈ univ.filter (fun a => D a = true), (p a - q a) := by\n  simp only [FinDist.probTrue, sum_sub_distrib]\n\n/-- `probTrue p D` is the total probability of the points that `D` accepts. -/\ntheorem FinDist.probTrue_eq (p : FinDist α) (D : α → Bool) :\n    p.probTrue D = ∑ a ∈ univ.filter (fun a => D a = true), p a :=\n  rfl\n\n",
        "raw_sha256": "db337beb6a90566b3a31da5efcd699e1353cd34f16db815b6d8d106c0923f719"
      }
    ],
    "interpretation": "FinDist adds documentation and acceptance-probability API, with no change to existing definitions/bodies; neither failing proof refers to those additions."
